Bicicletas públicas: recorridos realizados 2026, BA Data
--------------------------------------------------------

Datasets: trips (2,247,589 trips on Ecobici, Buenos Aires' public
bike-share, that started from 1 January to 30 September 2026, each with
its start, its length in minutes and the stations it started and ended
at) and stations (the 405 stations those trips start or end at, each with
its number, name and position)

Publisher: the Gobierno de la Ciudad de Buenos Aires, through BA Data,
the city's open data portal; the dataset "Bicicletas Públicas." of the
Secretaría de Transporte y Obras Públicas, Jefatura de Gabinete de
Ministros, its file "2026 - Recorridos realizados (ZIP)".
https://data.buenosaires.gob.ar/dataset/bicicletas-publicas

Terms: Creative Commons Attribution 2.5 Argentina. The portal's
catalogue record states the licence "CC-BY-2.5-AR" (license_id and
license_title); the build refuses to go on unless it still does and
still lists the file at the address below. SPDX does not list this
port, so the template names it LicenseRef-CC-BY-2.5-AR.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/ar/

Credit: "Ecobici trips, Gobierno de la Ciudad de Buenos Aires (BA Data),
CC BY 2.5 AR"

Version, and where and when: the catalogue record read on 2026-10-12 at
18:11 UTC (last changed 2026-10-08 21:35:49), the trip file at 18:30 UTC
(last modified Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:41:41 GMT, by the server's word; the
city replaces it monthly under the same address):

  https://data.buenosaires.gob.ar/api/3/action/package_show?id=bicicletas-publicas
  (81,234 bytes, SHA-256 1a5ff191248db9020260ac18349fe7026d3c7bcfeece8a3f6a61e2c710cb00af)
  https://cdn.buenosaires.gob.ar/datosabiertos/datasets/transporte-y-obras-publicas/bicicletas-publicas/recorridos-realizados-2026.zip
  (143,323,768 bytes, SHA-256 7e4c2c45d58bbc4ac638e1f6126f6d58872687f908e519851b489cb89fb1ce74;
  one file, trips.csv)

Modifications: of the file's 2,247,697 trip records, 2,247,589 are kept:
107 that start or end at the depot, "[Valet] Galpón", which the records
place at 0, 0, and one without a destination are left out. Of each trip
only the start (to the minute), the ride's length (in minutes, to a
tenth) and the two stations' numbers are kept; each rider's user number
and gender and the bicycle's model are not. The stations are taken from
the trips: each station's number, its name as most of its trips give it
and its position as most of its trips give it (six decimal places). The
map's SQL counts the trips between each pair of stations by part of the
day and weekday or weekend, and each station's departures and arrivals.


